load 0
=== commands and options
--- nextflow 
auth 	manage Seqera Platform authentication
clean 	clean up project cache and work directories
clone 	clone a project into a folder
config 	print a project configuration
console 	launch Nextflow interactive console
drop 	delete the local copy of a project
fs 	perform filesystem operations
help 	print the usage help for a command
info 	print project and system runtime information
inspect 	inspect process settings in a pipeline project
kuberun 	execute a workflow in a Kubernetes cluster (experimental)
launch 	launch a workflow in Seqera Platform
lineage 	explore workflows lineage metadata
lint 	lint Nextflow scripts and config files
list 	list all downloaded projects
log 	print executions log and runtime info
module 	manage Nextflow modules
plugin 	execute plugin-specific commands
pull 	download or update a project
run 	execute a pipeline project
secrets 	manage pipeline secrets
self-update 	update nextflow runtime to the latest available version
view 	view project script file(s)
--- nextflow ru
run 	execute a pipeline project
--- nextflow -
-C 	use the specified configuration file(s) overriding any defaults
-D 	set JVM properties
-bg 	execute nextflow in background
-c 	add the specified file to configuration set
-config 	add the specified file to configuration set
-config-ignore-includes 	disable the parsing of config includes
-h 	print help
-log 	set nextflow log file path
-q 	do not print information messages
-quiet 	do not print information messages
-remote-debug 	enable JVM interactive remote debugging
-syslog 	send logs to a syslog server
-trace 	enable trace level logging for the specified package name
-v 	print the program version
-version 	print the program version
--- nextflow -c 
custom.config 
nextflow.config 
nxf/
pipe/
results/
--- nextflow -c c
custom.config 
--- nextflow run -
-E 	export all current system environment
-N 	send a notification email on workflow completion
-ansi-log 	enable or disable ANSI console logging
-bucket-dir 	remote bucket where intermediate result files are stored
-cache 	enable or disable process caching
-d 	create a shallow clone of the specified depth
-deep 	create a shallow clone of the specified depth
-disable-jobs-cancellation 	prevent the cancellation of child jobs on termination
-dump-channels	dump channels for debugging purposes
-dump-hashes 	dump task hash keys for debugging purposes
-entry 	entry workflow name to be executed
-h 	print the command usage
-help 	print the command usage
-hub 	service hub where the project is hosted
-latest 	pull latest changes before run
-lib 	library extension path
-main-script 	the script file to be executed when launching a project
-name 	assign a mnemonic name to the pipeline run
-o 	directory where workflow outputs are stored
-offline 	do not check for remote project updates
-output-dir 	directory where workflow outputs are stored
-output-format 	output format for printing workflow outputs
-params-file 	load script parameters from a JSON/YAML file
-plugins 	plugins to be applied for this run
-preview 	run the workflow skipping the execution of all processes
-profile 	choose a configuration profile
-qs 	max number of processes executed in parallel by each executor
-queue-size 	max number of processes executed in parallel by each executor
-r 	revision of the project to run (branch, tag or commit)
-resume	execute the script using the cached results
-revision 	revision of the project to run (branch, tag or commit)
-stub 	execute the workflow replacing process scripts with stubs
-stub-run 	execute the workflow replacing process scripts with stubs
-test 	test a script function with the name specified
-user 	private repository user name
-w 	directory where intermediate result files are stored
-with-apptainer	enable process execution in an Apptainer container
-with-charliecloud	enable process execution in a Charliecloud container
-with-cloudcache	use an object storage bucket as storage for cache metadata
-with-conda	use the specified Conda environment package or file
-with-dag	create pipeline DAG file
-with-docker	enable process execution in a Docker container
-with-notification 	send a notification email on workflow completion
-with-podman	enable process execution in a Podman container
-with-report	create processes execution html report
-with-singularity	enable process execution in a Singularity container
-with-spack	use the specified Spack environment package or file
-with-timeline	create processes execution timeline file
-with-tower	monitor workflow execution with Seqera Platform
-with-trace	create processes execution tracing file
-with-weblog	send workflow status messages via HTTP to target URL
-without-conda 	disable the use of Conda environments
-without-docker 	disable process execution with Docker
-without-podman 	disable process execution in a Podman container
-without-spack 	disable the use of Spack environments
-work-dir 	directory where intermediate result files are stored
--- nextflow run -with-d
-with-dag	create pipeline DAG file
-with-docker	enable process execution in a Docker container
